2. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A PAID LICENCE

   "Commercial Use" means any of the following:

   (a) Selling, leasing, renting, or otherwise monetising hardware
       that runs this software.
   (b) Deploying the software in a facility, building, office,
       hotel, or any premises that generates revenue or is part of
       a commercial operation.
   (c) Providing a paid service that depends on this software —
       installation, integration, deployment, hosting, support,
       or managed operations.
   (d) Integrating the software into a product that is itself sold,
       distributed commercially, or offered as a service (whether
       or not the product or its source is open).
   (e) Offering the software as a paid SaaS, hosted service, or
       cloud service to third parties.

   None of the above is permitted without first obtaining a signed
   Commercial Licence from the copyright holder.


3. ROYALTIES AND LICENSING TERMS

